  "body": "## What changed\n\nStep 1, PR P of the UI plan #4245. A docked pane folds to its title, so that the viewport gets the space.\n\n- The fold flag is the `LeafNode::collapsed` flag of egui_dock. The fold arrow of the dock, the saved panel setups and the new fold law read this one flag.\n- A pane in a top-over-bottom stack folds natively to its tab bar.\n- A side pane (Browser at the left, Properties at the right) folds to a title chip, 28 points wide. The fold law keeps the open split fraction, holds the split at chip width on each frame, and puts the open fraction back on unfold. A window resize or a drag on the separator does not unfold or widen a folded pane.\n- The shell draws the chip in the folded leaf, under its tab bar. The chip shows the pane title, turned to read from top to bottom. One click on the chip unfolds the pane. The fold arrow of the dock also unfolds it.\n- Each chip keeps the safety state as text with a glyph (the #4245 E2 rule). The Browser chip shows the counts of blocked, stale and not generated operations, or \"Up to date\". The Properties chip shows the state of the open operation: \"Up to date\", \"Needs regenerate\", \"Not generated\" or \"Blocked\" (the reason is in the tooltip). The glyph is a check mark or a warning sign, so the state does not depend on colour. The sources are `status_of`, `stale_reason` and `tool_problem_of`, as in the tree and the operation page. Only a folded pane reads them.\n- The chip hover is a 2 px accent frame and a full-ink title. The tooltip follows the pointer.\n- Before this change, the fold arrow on a side pane did nothing. It now folds the pane. The viewport never folds: the fold law clears its flag. The viewport arrow stays visible and does nothing, because egui_dock 0.21.1 cannot hide the arrow on one leaf. The decision file records this, and the snap-back of a separator drag on a folded pane.\n- A saved panel setup keeps the folds and the open width of each folded side pane. It also writes the mark `camcraft_pane_folds`. A setup without the mark is from an older build and loads with all panes unfolded.\n- View > Reset layout and a setup load clear the stored widths. Reset gives the default layout with no pane folded.\n- The `show` path of the View door now also corrects the fold counts of the parent splits.\n\nFiles:\n- `crates/ui-kit/src/fold.rs` (new): the chip widget, the chip rect and the split fraction arithmetic. It holds no dock and no shell state.\n- `crates/ui/src/egui_app/layout/fold_state.rs` (new): the state line of each chip.\n- `crates/ui/src/egui_app/layout/fold.rs` (new): the fold law over the dock, the count fix-up (egui_dock keeps its own fix-up private), the chips, and the setup helpers.\n- `crates/ui/src/egui_app/layout/setups.rs`: the fold mark and the open widths in a saved setup.\n- `crates/ui/src/egui_app/shell.rs`: two small calls around `DockArea` (the fold law before, the chips after).\n- `crates/ui/src/state.rs`: one field, `pane_folds`.\n- `docs/decisions/4483-pane-fold.md`: the decisions.\n\nNo change to toolpaths, posts or the project file format. Layout is view state: no command and no history entry.\n\n## Pinning tests\n\n`crates/ui/src/egui_app/tests/pane_fold.rs` (new, in the `camcraft-ui` lib tests):\n- `the_browser_folds_to_a_chip_and_its_chip_unfolds_it` (the real fold arrow and the chip button)\n- `the_properties_pane_folds_at_the_right_and_the_arrow_unfolds_it`\n- `a_stacked_pane_folds_natively_to_its_tab_bar`\n- `a_separator_drag_does_not_unfold_a_folded_pane`\n- `a_window_resize_keeps_the_fold_at_chip_width`\n- `the_viewport_never_folds`\n- `reset_layout_unfolds_every_pane`\n- `a_saved_setup_keeps_its_folds_and_their_open_width`\n- `an_older_setup_loads_with_every_pane_unfolded`\n- `a_stale_operation_shows_on_the_folded_browser_chip`\n- `the_folded_properties_chip_names_the_operation_state`\n- `a_fold_does_not_move_the_camera`\n\nLayout test: `page_layout::layout_shell_folded` (1366 x 768, both side panes folded).\n\nKit tests in `camcraft_ui_kit::fold::tests` (7 tests: the fraction arithmetic, the chip rect, a click on the chip, the hover step in the dark and the light theme with `contrast::ratio`, and the glyph of the state line).\n\n`crates/ui` `#[test]` count: 2019 before, 2032 after. No snapshot PNG changes.\n\n## Gate\n\nOn the final head `1bca29cc9` (lanes, winbuild, Windows; log `gate-4483-1bca29cc9.log`, first line `head 1bca29cc94a3683e8374f85bbcf4d3b75c529307`):\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base origin/main`: 20 steps, 0 failed, 0 stalled (`ui-kit suites: lib` ok, `ui build` ok, `ui suites: lib` ok, all 16 `ui suites` binaries ok). The `site tests` step is SKIPPED on that lane (python, zola and node are not installed). That is not a pass. The diff does not change the site.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-ui-kit -p camcraft-ui --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n\nThe head before it, `ff940f580`, has the same code with LF line ends in `shell.rs`. On it, `cargo xtask gate test pane_fold --crate camcraft-ui` (all `pane_fold` tests), the same quick gate and clippy also passed. `1bca29cc9` only puts the CRLF line ends of `shell.rs` back, so that the diff shows the 9 changed lines and does not conflict with #4490.\n\nAn earlier head (`485c9d934`) failed three `pane_fold` tests with `Harness::run exceeded max_steps`: the fold law asked for a repaint on each frame. Head `669c595aa` fixes it. The light lane and the example catalog suites do not apply: no post and no toolpath changed.\n\n## Screenshots\n\n1366 x 768, the seeded shell, Contour1 open in Properties.\n\nBefore (all panes open):\n\n![before](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/qsmits/Camcraft/pr-screenshots/4492/before.png)\n\nAfter (both side panes folded, the job up to date):\n\n![after](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/qsmits/Camcraft/pr-screenshots/4492/after.png)\n\nAfter (folded, Contour1 edited and now stale: the chips say \"1 stale\" and \"Needs regenerate\"):\n\n![after-stale](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/qsmits/Camcraft/pr-screenshots/4492/after-stale.png)\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- A fold in a floating window. Only the main area folds side panes; a float keeps the egui_dock behaviour.\n- No MCP tool: a fold is view state, not a command.\n\nChangelog: Docked side panes (Browser, Properties) fold to a narrow title chip with the fold arrow of their tab bar, and unfold with one click on the chip; a folded chip still shows the operation state (stale counts, \"Needs regenerate\"); saved panel setups keep the folds.\n\nEffort: medium\n\nFixes #4483\n",
